Third-party data
----------------

The recorded API responses in src/tekmerion/demo/fixtures/ are kept so that the demo
and the tests run offline. They are not covered by the Apache License; each keeps the
terms of its source:

- ClinicalTrials.gov (National Library of Medicine) and openFDA drug labels (Food
  and Drug Administration): United States government data.
- Crossref metadata: bibliographic facts, which Crossref makes available without
  restriction.
- PubMed and PubTator (National Library of Medicine): bibliographic records, and
  abstracts only of the records the demo, the tests and the evaluation fetch; the
  recorder removes every other PubMed abstract. Abstracts remain under the copyright
  of their publishers or authors.
- Europe PMC search results: an abstract is kept only when Europe PMC lists the
  article under CC BY or CC0, or when the result is the lookup of a record the demo
  or the evaluation fetches. The recorder removes every other abstract.
- Full text: Jiao B, Sato R, Mak J, et al. Financial risk protection from vaccines
  in 52 Gavi-eligible low- and middle-income countries: a modeling study. PLoS
  Medicine. 2025. doi:10.1371/journal.pmed.1004764. Licensed under CC BY 4.0
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/), recorded unmodified from Europe
  PMC (PMC12585062).
- Preprint: Garba A, Usman S, Hussaini A. Mapping immune targets in peste des petits
  ruminants virus hemagglutinin: an integrated computational framework for vaccine
  candidate prioritization. Research Square. 2026. doi:10.21203/rs.3.rs-10665898/v1.
  Licensed under CC BY 4.0.

A rights holder who wants a recorded item removed can open an issue in the
repository.
